# Completion at point's auto popup (docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md), on
# the shared config, under the Vim scheme that ships. The headless mode's job
# clock is fake: a pause of 240 ms fires only when the script advances it.
reload
settle
resize 640 480
key i KeyI -
commit alpha alpine beta
# RET with no session breaks the line; `a` and `l` are typed, and each
# re-arms the pause of the shipped `words` source.
key <Enter> Enter -
key a KeyA -
key l KeyL -
settle
# The pause fires: the session of `words` opens with nothing chosen, and its
# job lists the words of the open buffers that match `al`.
advance 240
join
scene
# C-n chooses the first and previews it in the region.
key n KeyN control
scene
# RET accepts it: the list closes and the window is full height again.
key <Enter> Enter -
scene
